  "claim": "Bryan Douglas Caplan is an adjunct scholar. He works where Patrick Michaels is a senior fellow in Washington D.C.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Bryan Caplan. Sentence: Bryan Douglas Caplan (born April 8, 1971) is an American economist.\nPage: Bryan Caplan. Sentence: Caplan is a professor of economics at George Mason University, research fellow at the Mercatus Center, adjunct scholar at the Cato Institute, and frequent contributor to Freakonomics as well as publishing his own blog, EconLog.\nPage: Cato Institute. Sentence: The Cato Institute is an American libertarian think tank headquartered in Washington, D.C. It was founded as the Charles Koch Foundation in 1974 by Ed Crane, Murray Rothbard, and Charles Koch, chairman of the board and chief executive officer of the conglomerate Koch Industries.\nPage: Patrick Michaels. Sentence: Michaels is a senior fellow in environmental studies at the Cato Institute.",
