        "original_id": "6f80b03b-ff08-5b53-8d5b-2dbab7c44725",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Bryan Caplan, Ed Crane, Murray Rothbard, Charles Koch, Patrick Michaels\n- Organizations: George Mason University, Mercatus Center, Cato Institute, Koch Industries\n- Roles: economist, professor of economics, research fellow, adjunct scholar, senior fellow, contributor\n- Places: Washington, D.C.\n- Topics: libertarian think tank, environmental studies, EconLog, Freakonomics\n\nFacts:\n- Bryan Douglas Caplan was born on April 8, 1971, and he is an American economist.\n- The Cato Institute was founded in 1974 as the Charles Koch Foundation by Ed Crane, Murray Rothbard, and Charles Koch.\n- The Cato Institute is an American libertarian think tank headquartered in Washington, D.C.\n- Charles Koch is chairman of the board and chief executive officer of Koch Industries.\n- Bryan Caplan is a professor of economics at George Mason University.\n- Bryan Caplan is a research fellow at the Mercatus Center.\n- Bryan Caplan is an adjunct scholar at the Cato Institute.\n- Bryan Caplan is a frequent contributor to Freakonomics and publishes his own blog, EconLog.\n- Patrick Michaels is a senior fellow in environmental studies at the Cato Institute.",
